<title>UK: British Airways says taking cargo bookings.</title>
<headline>British Airways says taking cargo bookings.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways said its World Cargo air freight unit is now taking bookings for all services following last week's strike by cabin crew which badly disrupted schedules.</p>
<p>The only exceptions, said a spokesman, were live animals and human remains, for which bookings would not be taken for the time being.</p>
<p>This was because services were not yet completely back to normal and delays might still occur.</p>
<p>BA flights were 85 percent normal from London Heathrow on Monday morning and a full schedule was expected to be operating by Wednesday, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>He said BA did not accept cargo bookings for flights during the 72-hour strike period and therefore had no cargo backlog to clear.</p>
</text>
